  "name": "C-ACE",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "C-ACE was a small convention held in Ottawa, Ontario, most often in early June. It was founded in 2002 as the Canadian Anthro and Cartooning Expo, later the Canadian Art and Cartooning Expo, and finally simply C-ACE. It focused on learning across visual art, writing, costuming and music, in anthro and other genres, and kept a \"clean\" rating, with artwork limited to PG-13 at most. Six editions were held between 2002 and 2007, with attendance between 110 and 224, and a popular Sketch Pad Lounge.",
